{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w1-fixture.c; nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w1-errno.scm | sed -n '45,240p'; nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w2-fixture.c\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w1-fixture.c; nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w1-errno.scm | sed -n '45,240p'; nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w2-fixture.c\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t/* W1 fixture — errno-atomicity call shapes.\n     2\t *\n     3\t * p1a-r2 REPAIR of review finding F2 (the P1a shims read errno AFTER malloc\n     4\t * and shapes A/C manufactured the expected errno after the \"target\" returned,\n     5\t * which cannot qualify capture-before-allocation).\n     6\t *\n     7\t * EVERY shim below follows the astra essential sequence exactly:\n     8\t *\n     9\t *   target call  ->  int saved = errno;   IMMEDIATELY, before ANY\n    10\t *                 ->  malloc / conversion / cleanup / Scheme re-entry\n    11\t *                 ->  the pair travels out as one malloc'd struct\n    12\t *\n    13\t * The TARGETS own their errno (like real syscalls) — the shims never\n    14\t * manufacture one after the fact:\n    15\t *   w1_target_a sets EAGAIN itself and returns -1 (failure);\n    16\t *   w1_target_c sets EACCES itself and returns -2 (failure);\n    17\t *   w1_target_b is a SUCCESS that must preserve the caller's errno = 42\n    18\t *   (contract: do not normalize success to zero).\n    19\t *\n    20\t * Capture-order negative controls (the reviewer's required addition —\n    21\t * capture position must be load-bearing, i.e. observable):\n    22\t *   shape F: an intervening clobber (errno = W1_INTERVENING_CLOBBER) is\n    23\t *            written BETWEEN the target call and the use of the captured\n    24\t *            value; the immediate capture MUST defeat it — the Scheme side\n    25\t *            asserts the TARGET's errno, never the clobber.\n    26\t *   shape G: a deliberately WRONG shim that captures AFTER the intervening\n    27\t *            clobber; the witness asserts it yields the CLOBBERED value.\n    28\t *            This proves the assertions can distinguish capture order at\n    29\t *            all: a harness in which G also reported the target's errno\n    30\t *            would be insensitive, and the immediate-capture shapes would\n    31\t *            not be load-bearing.\n    32\t *\n    33\t * The pair travels out of the shim as one malloc'd struct, so the Scheme\n    34\t * side reads result and errno from a single allocation — no second read of\n    35\t * errno can intervene. A global \"last errno\" cell would fail the interleaved\n    36\t * and threaded iterations; re-reading errno after any cleanup would fail the\n    37\t * post-capture clobber; capturing after malloc (the F2 defect) would fail\n    38\t * shape F's intervening clobber whenever malloc touches errno.\n    39\t */\n    40\t\n    41\t#include <errno.h>\n    42\t#include <stdlib.h>\n    43\t#include <stdio.h>\n    44\t\n    45\t/* c-define'd in w1-errno.scm */\n    46\textern int w1_nested_cb (int x);\n    47\t\n    48\t#define W1_INTERVENING_CLOBBER 4242\n    49\t#define W1_POST_CAPTURE_CLOBBER 7777\n    50\t\n    51\ttypedef struct { int res; int err; } w1_pair;\n    52\t\n    53\tstatic int w1_target_a (void) { errno = EAGAIN; return -1; }  /* failure: target's OWN errno */\n    54\tstatic int w1_target_b (void) { return 7; }                   /* success: errno 42 preserved */\n    55\tstatic int w1_target_c (void) { errno = EACCES; return -2; }  /* failure: target's OWN errno */\n    56\t\n    57\t/* shape A: failure; the target's real EAGAIN must survive allocation */\n    58\tw1_pair *w1_shape_a (void)\n    59\t{\n    60\t  int r;\n    61\t  int saved;\n    62\t  w1_pair *p;\n    63\t  errno = 0;\n    64\t  r = w1_target_a ();\n    65\t  saved = errno;                    /* capture IMMEDIATELY after the target */\n    66\t  p = malloc (sizeof (w1_pair));    /* allocation AFTER capture */\n    67\t  p->res = r;\n    68\t  p->err = saved;\n    69\t  errno = W1_POST_CAPTURE_CLOBBER;  /* deliberate post-capture clobber */\n    70\t  return p;\n    71\t}\n    72\t\n    73\t/* shape B: success that PRESERVES errno = 42 (contract: do not normalize\n    74\t   success to zero); capture still immediately after the target */\n    75\tw1_pair *w1_shape_b (void)\n    76\t{\n    77\t  int r;\n    78\t  int saved;\n    79\t  w1_pair *p;\n    80\t  errno = 42;\n    81\t  r = w1_target_b ();\n    82\t  saved = errno;                    /* capture IMMEDIATELY, success included */\n    83\t  p = malloc (sizeof (w1_pair));\n    84\t  p->res = r;\n    85\t  p->err = saved;\n    86\t  errno = W1_POST_CAPTURE_CLOBBER;\n    87\t  return p;\n    88\t}\n    89\t\n    90\t/* shape C: failure; the target's real EACCES must survive allocation */\n    91\tw1_pair *w1_shape_c (void)\n    92\t{\n    93\t  int r;\n    94\t  int saved;\n    95\t  w1_pair *p;\n    96\t  errno = 0;\n    97\t  r = w1_target_c ();\n    98\t  saved = errno;                    /* capture IMMEDIATELY after the target */\n    99\t  p = malloc (sizeof (w1_pair));\n   100\t  p->res = r;\n   101\t  p->err = saved;\n   102\t  errno = W1_POST_CAPTURE_CLOBBER;\n   103\t  return p;\n   104\t}\n   105\t\n   106\t/* shape D: like C, but the c-lambda body adds an ___AT_END clobber that runs\n   107\t   AFTER the result conversion — the captured pair must not change. */\n   108\t\n   109\t/* shape E: nested calls. Captures EIO BEFORE any allocation and BEFORE the\n   110\t   re-entry into Scheme via the c-define'd callback w1_nested_cb (which\n   111\t   itself performs a nested foreign call and clobbers errno through its own\n   112\t   shim), then returns the pair captured BEFORE the re-entry. A shim that\n   113\t   allocated first or re-read errno after the nested call would show the\n   114\t   callback's post-clobber value instead of EIO. */\n   115\tw1_pair *w1_shape_e (void)\n   116\t{\n   117\t  w1_pair *p;\n   118\t  int saved;\n   119\t  int cb;\n   120\t  errno = EIO;\n   121\t  saved = errno;                    /* capture IMMEDIATELY, before ANY malloc */\n   122\t  p = malloc (sizeof (w1_pair));\n   123\t  p->res = -3;\n   124\t  p->err = saved;\n   125\t  cb = w1_nested_cb (5);            /* re-enter Scheme; inner shim B runs inside */\n   126\t  if (cb != 12)                     /* callback sanity: must return exactly 12 */\n   127\t    {\n   128\t      p->res = -999;\n   129\t      p->err = cb;\n   130\t    }\n   131\t  errno = W1_POST_CAPTURE_CLOBBER;  /* deliberate post-capture clobber */\n   132\t  return p;\n   133\t}\n   134\t\n   135\t/* shape F: intervening-clobber negative control (GOOD order). The clobber\n   136\t   lands BETWEEN the target call and the use of the captured value; the\n   137\t   immediate capture defeats it. */\n   138\tw1_pair *w1_shape_f (void)\n   139\t{\n   140\t  int r;\n   141\t  int saved;\n   142\t  w1_pair *p;\n   143\t  errno = 0;\n   144\t  r = w1_target_a ();\n   145\t  saved = errno;                    /* immediate capture ... */\n   146\t  errno = W1_INTERVENING_CLOBBER;   /* ... defeats this intervening clobber */\n   147\t  p = malloc (sizeof (w1_pair));\n   148\t  p->res = r;\n   149\t  p->err = saved;                   /* the TARGET's errno, never the clobber */\n   150\t  errno = W1_POST_CAPTURE_CLOBBER;\n   151\t  return p;\n   152\t}\n   153\t\n   154\t/* shape G: intervening-clobber negative control (deliberately WRONG order —\n   155\t   captures AFTER the clobber). The witness asserts this shim reports the\n   156\t   CLOBBERED value: proof that the assertions distinguish capture order. */\n   157\tw1_pair *w1_shape_g (void)\n   158\t{\n   159\t  int r;\n   160\t  int saved;\n   161\t  w1_pair *p;\n   162\t  errno = 0;\n   163\t  r = w1_target_a ();\n   164\t  errno = W1_INTERVENING_CLOBBER;   /* intervening clobber ... */\n   165\t  saved = errno;                    /* ... captured AFTER it (wrong order) */\n   166\t  p = malloc (sizeof (w1_pair));\n   167\t  p->res = r;\n   168\t  p->err = saved;                   /* the clobber leaks in — by design */\n   169\t  return p;\n   170\t}\n   171\t\n   172\tvoid w1_free_pair (w1_pair *p) { free (p); }\n   173\t\n   174\t/* Platform errno values probed by the Scheme side so the assertions hold on\n   175\t   any OS (EAGAIN/EACCES/EIO differ between macOS and Linux), plus the\n   176\t   intervening-clobber constant so the negative-control assertion compares\n   177\t   against the C-declared value, not a Scheme-side magic number. */\n   178\tint w1_errno_again (void) { return EAGAIN; }\n   179\tint w1_errno_acces (void) { return EACCES; }\n   180\tint w1_errno_io    (void) { return EIO; }\n   181\tint w1_intervening_clobber (void) { return W1_INTERVENING_CLOBBER; }\n    45\tint w1_intervening_clobber (void);\n    46\t\n    47\tc-declare-end\n    48\t)\n    49\t\n    50\t(c-define-type w1-pair (pointer \"w1_pair\"))\n    51\t\n    52\t;; platform errno values (EAGAIN/EACCES/EIO differ between macOS and Linux)\n    53\t(define w1-EAGAIN ((c-lambda () int \"w1_errno_again\")))\n    54\t(define w1-EACCES ((c-lambda () int \"w1_errno_acces\")))\n    55\t(define w1-EIO    ((c-lambda () int \"w1_errno_io\")))\n    56\t;; the intervening-clobber constant (C-declared, so the negative control\n    57\t;; compares against the fixture's own value)\n    58\t(define w1-clobber ((c-lambda () int \"w1_intervening_clobber\")))\n    59\t\n    60\t(define w1-call-a (c-lambda () w1-pair \"w1_shape_a\"))\n    61\t(define w1-call-b (c-lambda () w1-pair \"w1_shape_b\"))\n    62\t(define w1-call-c (c-lambda () w1-pair \"w1_shape_c\"))\n    63\t(define w1-call-e (c-lambda () w1-pair \"w1_shape_e\"))\n    64\t(define w1-call-f (c-lambda () w1-pair \"w1_shape_f\"))\n    65\t(define w1-call-g (c-lambda () w1-pair \"w1_shape_g\"))\n    66\t\n    67\t;; shape D: c-lambda code body, ___AT_END clobber after result conversion.\n    68\t(define w1-call-d\n    69\t  (c-lambda () w1-pair\n    70\t#<<c-lambda-end\n    71\t   w1_pair *p = w1_shape_c ();\n    72\t   ___return (p);\n    73\t   #define ___AT_END errno = 31337;\n    74\tc-lambda-end\n    75\t))\n    76\t\n    77\t(define w1-pair-res (c-lambda (w1-pair) int \"___return (___arg1->res);\"))\n    78\t(define w1-pair-err (c-lambda (w1-pair) int \"___return (___arg1->err);\"))\n    79\t(define w1-free-pair (c-lambda (w1-pair) void \"w1_free_pair (___arg1); ___return;\"))\n    80\t\n    81\t;; c-define'd callback used by shape E: performs a nested foreign call\n    82\t;; (shape B) and returns exactly 12 when x = 5.\n    83\t(c-define (w1-nested-cb x) (int) int \"w1_nested_cb\" \"extern\"\n    84\t  (if (= x 5)\n    85\t      (let ((p (w1-call-b)))\n    86\t        (let ((r (+ (w1-pair-res p) (w1-pair-err p))))  ; 7 + 42, forces both reads\n    87\t          (w1-free-pair p)\n    88\t          (if (= r 49) 12 r)))\n    89\t      -1))\n    90\t\n    91\t(define w1-failures 0)\n    92\t(define w1-checks 0)\n    93\t\n    94\t(define (w1-check! tag p er es)\n    95\t  (set! w1-checks (+ w1-checks 1))\n    96\t  (let ((r (w1-pair-res p)) (e (w1-pair-err p)))\n    97\t    (if (not (and (= r er) (= e es)))\n    98\t        (begin\n    99\t          (set! w1-failures (+ w1-failures 1))\n   100\t          (display \"W1-MISMATCH: \") (display tag)\n   101\t          (display \" got (\") (display r) (display \",\") (display e)\n   102\t          (display \") expected (\") (display er) (display \",\") (display es)\n   103\t          (display \")\")\n   104\t          (newline)))\n   105\t    (w1-free-pair p)))\n   106\t\n   107\t(define (w1-loop! tag call er es n)\n   108\t  (let loop ((i 0))\n   109\t    (if (< i n)\n   110\t        (begin\n   111\t          (w1-check! tag (call) er es)\n   112\t          (loop (+ i 1))))))\n   113\t\n   114\t(define (w1-worker tid)\n   115\t  ;; interleaved shapes from one thread; a global \"last errno\" cell cannot\n   116\t  ;; survive this interleave, per-invocation capture must — and a shim that\n   117\t  ;; captured late (after allocation) would fail A/F vs G's different values.\n   118\t  (let loop ((i 0))\n   119\t    (if (< i 400)\n   120\t        (begin\n   121\t          (w1-check! \"A\" (w1-call-a) -1 w1-EAGAIN)\n   122\t          (w1-check! \"B\" (w1-call-b) 7 42)\n   123\t          (w1-check! \"C\" (w1-call-c) -2 w1-EACCES)\n   124\t          (w1-check! \"E\" (w1-call-e) -3 w1-EIO)\n   125\t          (w1-check! \"F\" (w1-call-f) -1 w1-EAGAIN)\n   126\t          (w1-check! \"G\" (w1-call-g) -1 w1-clobber)\n   127\t          (thread-sleep! 0.0001)              ; force green interleaving\n   128\t          (loop (+ i 1))))))\n   129\t\n   130\t(display \"=== W1 errno-atomicity witness (p1a-r2: capture-before-allocation + negative controls) ===\")\n   131\t(newline)\n   132\t(display \"EAGAIN=\") (display w1-EAGAIN) (display \" EACCES=\") (display w1-EACCES)\n   133\t(display \" EIO=\") (display w1-EIO) (display \" intervening-clobber=\") (display w1-clobber)\n   134\t(newline)\n   135\t(set! w1-failures 0)\n   136\t(set! w1-checks 0)\n   137\t\n   138\t;; negative control FIRST: the deliberately-late shim must observe the\n   139\t;; clobber, or the assertions would be insensitive to capture order.\n   140\t(let ((p (w1-call-g)))\n   141\t  (let ((r (w1-pair-res p)) (e (w1-pair-err p)))\n   142\t    (w1-free-pair p)\n   143\t    (set! w1-checks (+ w1-checks 1))\n   144\t    (if (and (= r -1) (= e w1-clobber))\n   145\t        (begin\n   146\t          (display \"W1-NEGATIVE-CONTROL: OK (shape G captured AFTER the intervening clobber and reported it — the assertions distinguish capture order, so the immediate-capture shapes are load-bearing)\")\n   147\t          (newline))\n   148\t        (begin\n   149\t          (set! w1-failures (+ w1-failures 1))\n   150\t          (display \"W1-NEGATIVE-CONTROL: FAIL (shape G got (\") (display r)\n   151\t          (display \",\") (display e) (display \") expected (\") (display -1)\n   152\t          (display \",\") (display w1-clobber)\n   153\t          (display \") — assertions insensitive to capture order)\")\n   154\t          (newline)))))\n   155\t\n   156\t;; sequential shapes\n   157\t(w1-loop! \"A\" w1-call-a -1 w1-EAGAIN 200)\n   158\t(w1-loop! \"B\" w1-call-b 7 42 200)\n   159\t(w1-loop! \"C\" w1-call-c -2 w1-EACCES 200)\n   160\t(w1-loop! \"D\" w1-call-d -2 w1-EACCES 100)      ; ___AT_END clobber must not leak\n   161\t(w1-loop! \"E\" w1-call-e -3 w1-EIO 100)         ; nested re-entry capture\n   162\t(w1-loop! \"F\" w1-call-f -1 w1-EAGAIN 200)      ; intervening clobber DEFEATED\n   163\t(w1-loop! \"G\" w1-call-g -1 w1-clobber 100)     ; late capture reports the clobber\n   164\t\n   165\t;; concurrent shapes from two Scheme threads\n   166\t(define t1 (make-thread (lambda () (w1-worker 1)) 'w1-t1))\n   167\t(define t2 (make-thread (lambda () (w1-worker 2)) 'w1-t2))\n   168\t(thread-start! t1)\n   169\t(thread-start! t2)\n   170\t(thread-join! t1)\n   171\t(thread-join! t2)\n   172\t\n   173\t(display \"W1-CHECKS=\") (display w1-checks) (newline)\n   174\t(display \"W1-FAILURES=\") (display w1-failures) (newline)\n   175\t(if (= w1-failures 0)\n   176\t    (display \"W1-VERDICT: PASS (every shim captured (result,errno) immediately after the target, before ANY allocation/conversion/re-entry: shapes A/C preserve the target's own errno, shape B preserves errno=42 on success, shape E captures before the nested Scheme re-entry, shape F defeats an intervening clobber written between target and capture; shape G proves the assertions distinguish capture order; the ___AT_END clobber (shape D) and the two-thread interleave add conversion-boundary and scheduling pressure)\")\n   177\t    (display \"W1-VERDICT: FAIL\"))\n   178\t(newline)\n     1\t/* W2 fixture — the blocking-call shape with an OBSERVABLE release handshake.\n     2\t *\n     3\t * p1a-r2 REPAIR of review finding F3 (the P1a handshake existed in C but was\n     4\t * never called from Scheme, and the witness printed its verdict\n     5\t * unconditionally).\n     6\t *\n     7\t * w2_block blocks on a handshake that ONLY a call to w2_release_handshake()\n     8\t * can end early; a C-side deadline bounds the block so a build that cannot\n     9\t * release converts what is otherwise a permanent deadlock into structured\n    10\t * evidence. The external watchdog (watchdog.sh) is the second line of\n    11\t * defense and its exit 124 is an INDEPENDENT timeout detection — always a\n    12\t * recorded failure.\n    13\t *\n    14\t * Everything the Scheme witness needs to DERIVE its verdict from observed\n    15\t * state (never an unconditional print) is exported:\n    16\t *   w2_block(deadline)  returns the OBSERVED release cause:\n    17\t *                         0 = released by a w2_release_handshake() call,\n    18\t *                         1 = the C-side deadline fired first\n    19\t *   w2_release_handshake()  counts its calls and whether any arrived while\n    20\t *                           the wait was still active (w2_handshake_calls,\n    21\t *                           w2_handshake_during_block)\n    22\t *   w2_in_block_p()     the live in-block flag, so the Scheme side can\n    23\t *                       observe \"round started while C was blocked\" directly\n    24\t *                       from the C fixture's own state\n    25\t *   w2_block_blocked_ms()  how long the block actually lasted\n    26\t *\n    27\t * The real collection used by the witness goes through the documented runtime\n    28\t * API gambit.h:14772-14774:\n    29\t *   ___IMP_FUNC(___BOOL,___garbage_collect)\n    30\t *      ___P((___PSD ___SIZE_TS requested_words_still),());\n    31\t */\n    32\t\n    33\t#include <stdio.h>\n    34\t#include <errno.h>\n    35\t#include <time.h>\n    36\t#include <pthread.h>\n    37\t\n    38\tstatic pthread_mutex_t w2_mu = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;\n    39\tstatic pthread_cond_t  w2_cv = PTHREAD_COND_INITIALIZER;\n    40\tstatic int w2_proceed = 0;\n    41\tstatic int w2_wait_active = 0;\n    42\tstatic int w2_in_block = 0;\n    43\tstatic int w2_handshake_calls = 0;\n    44\tstatic int w2_handshake_during_block = 0;\n    45\tstatic long w2_blocked_ms = 0;\n    46\t\n    47\tint w2_block (int deadline_seconds)\n    48\t{\n    49\t  struct timespec ts;\n    50\t  struct timespec t0, t1;\n    51\t  int cause = 1;   /* deadline, unless a handshake ends the wait */\n    52\t\n    53\t  clock_gettime (CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &t0);\n    54\t  clock_gettime (CLOCK_REALTIME, &ts);\n    55\t  ts.tv_sec += deadline_seconds;\n    56\t\n    57\t  w2_in_block = 1;\n    58\t  fprintf (stdout, \"W2C: foreign call ENTERED, blocking on handshake (deadline %ds)\\n\",\n    59\t           deadline_seconds);\n    60\t  fflush (stdout);\n    61\t\n    62\t  pthread_mutex_lock (&w2_mu);\n    63\t  w2_wait_active = 1;\n    64\t  while (!w2_proceed)\n    65\t    {\n    66\t      int r = pthread_cond_timedwait (&w2_cv, &w2_mu, &ts);\n    67\t      if (r == ETIMEDOUT)\n    68\t        break;\n    69\t    }\n    70\t  if (w2_proceed)\n    71\t    cause = 0;\n    72\t  w2_wait_active = 0;\n    73\t  pthread_mutex_unlock (&w2_mu);\n    74\t\n    75\t  w2_in_block = 0;\n    76\t  clock_gettime (CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &t1);\n    77\t  w2_blocked_ms = (long) (t1.tv_sec - t0.tv_sec) * 1000\n    78\t                + (t1.tv_nsec - t0.tv_nsec) / 1000000;\n    79\t\n    80\t  fprintf (stdout, \"W2C: foreign call RETURNING (cause=%s, blocked %ldms)\\n\",\n    81\t           cause == 0 ? \"handshake\" : \"deadline\", w2_blocked_ms);\n    82\t  fflush (stdout);\n    83\t  return cause;\n    84\t}\n    85\t\n    86\t/* The release handshake. Called FROM SCHEME (via c-lambda) in the qualify\n    87\t   mode — the qualification design releases C only after the contender has\n    88\t   completed a REAL collection; on a build where the contender cannot run\n    89\t   while C is blocked, the handshake provably cannot arrive during the block,\n    90\t   which is exactly what the counters record. */\n    91\tvoid w2_release_handshake (void)\n    92\t{\n    93\t  pthread_mutex_lock (&w2_mu);\n    94\t  w2_handshake_calls++;\n    95\t  if (w2_wait_active)\n    96\t    w2_handshake_during_block++;\n    97\t  w2_proceed = 1;\n    98\t  pthread_cond_broadcast (&w2_cv);\n    99\t  pthread_mutex_unlock (&w2_mu);\n   100\t}\n   101\t\n   102\tint w2_handshake_calls_total (void) { return w2_handshake_calls; }\n   103\tint w2_handshake_during_block_total (void) { return w2_handshake_during_block; }\n   104\tint w2_in_block_p (void) { return w2_in_block; }\n   105\tint w2_block_blocked_ms (void) { return (int) w2_blocked_ms; }\n   106\t\n   107\tint w2_noblock (void)\n   108\t{\n   109\t  fprintf (stdout, \"W2C: non-blocking foreign call entered+returned\\n\");\n   110\t  fflush (stdout);\n   111\t  return 1;\n   112\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
