{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w2-blocking.scm | sed -n '35,240p'; nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w3-fthread.c | sed -n '30,310p'; nl -ba p1a/witnesses/w3-server.scm | sed -n '1,110p'\"","aggregated_output":"    35\t;;     during the block, and the witness-object mutations survived real\n    36\t;;     collections. On the provisioned single-processor build B cannot\n    37\t;;     execute while C is blocked, so the OBSERVED verdict is FAIL with the\n    38\t;;     facts recorded (release-cause=deadline, rounds-during-block=0,\n    39\t;;     handshake-during-block=no) — the documented refusal evidence. The\n    40\t;;     internal-consistency guards (round counts, handshake counts, witness\n    41\t;;     slots) turn any incoherent observation into FAIL-INCONSISTENT with a\n    42\t;;     nonzero exit.\n    43\t;;\n    44\t;;   ./w2.exe -:d5 blocked\n    45\t;;     STARVATION DEMONSTRATION — the P1a variant, kept as a documented\n    46\t;;     diagnostic: B is started only AFTER A has entered the blocking call,\n    47\t;;     so on this build every B round can only run after C returns. The\n    48\t;;     verdict is derived from the same observed-state counters\n    49\t;;     (rounds-during-block, in-block flag, blocked duration); an\n    50\t;;     unexpected B progression during the block is flagged UNEXPECTED.\n    51\t\n    52\t(c-declare #<<c-declare-end\n    53\t\n    54\tint w2_block (int deadline_seconds);\n    55\tvoid w2_release_handshake (void);\n    56\tint w2_noblock (void);\n    57\tint w2_handshake_calls_total (void);\n    58\tint w2_handshake_during_block_total (void);\n    59\tint w2_in_block_p (void);\n    60\tint w2_block_blocked_ms (void);\n    61\t\n    62\tc-declare-end\n    63\t)\n    64\t\n    65\t(define w2-block   (c-lambda (int) int \"w2_block\"))\n    66\t(define w2-noblock (c-lambda () int \"w2_noblock\"))\n    67\t(define w2-release-handshake (c-lambda () void \"w2_release_handshake\"))\n    68\t(define w2-handshake-calls (c-lambda () int \"w2_handshake_calls_total\"))\n    69\t(define w2-handshake-during-block (c-lambda () int \"w2_handshake_during_block_total\"))\n    70\t(define w2-in-block-p (c-lambda () int \"w2_in_block_p\"))\n    71\t(define w2-blocked-ms (c-lambda () int \"w2_block_blocked_ms\"))\n    72\t;; REAL collection through the documented C API (gambit.h ~14769):\n    73\t;;   ___IMP_FUNC(___BOOL,___garbage_collect)\n    74\t;;      ___P((___PSD ___SIZE_TS requested_words_still),());\n    75\t(define w2-real-gc\n    76\t  (c-lambda () int\n    77\t    \"___return (___EXT(___garbage_collect) (___PSP 0) ? 1 : 0);\"))\n    78\t\n    79\t(define (w2-now) (time->seconds (current-time)))\n    80\t(define (w2-log . parts)\n    81\t  ;; one forced-flush line, so the ordering with the C fixture's\n    82\t  ;; stdout prints (also flushed) is exact in the recorded output.\n    83\t  (for-each display parts)\n    84\t  (newline)\n    85\t  (force-output))\n    86\t\n    87\t;; ---- observed-state variables (reset per mode) --------------------------\n    88\t\n    89\t(define w2-witness-obj (make-vector 4 0)) ; LIVE ROOTED object mutated by B\n    90\t(define w2-b-executing #f)                ; set by B's FIRST action\n    91\t(define w2-a-entering #f)                 ; set by A before entering C\n    92\t(define w2-c-returned #f)                 ; set by A after the C call returned\n    93\t(define w2-rounds-during-block 0)         ; B rounds STARTED while C was blocked\n    94\t(define w2-rounds-after 0)                ; B rounds started after C returned\n    95\t(define w2-rounds-overlapping 0)          ; control: B rounds started while A\n    96\t                                          ; had completed <3 calls\n    97\t(define w2-handshake-called #f)           ; did SCHEME call the handshake?\n    98\t(define w2-a-calls-done 0)                ; control: A's completed call count\n    99\t\n   100\t(define (w2-reset-state!)\n   101\t  (set! w2-witness-obj (make-vector 4 0))\n   102\t  (set! w2-b-executing #f)\n   103\t  (set! w2-a-entering #f)\n   104\t  (set! w2-c-returned #f)\n   105\t  (set! w2-rounds-during-block 0)\n   106\t  (set! w2-rounds-after 0)\n   107\t  (set! w2-rounds-overlapping 0)\n   108\t  (set! w2-handshake-called #f)\n   109\t  (set! w2-a-calls-done 0))\n   110\t\n   111\t(define (w2-mutate-witness! i)\n   112\t  ;; mutate the LIVE ROOTED witness object; the slots must hold the correct\n   113\t  ;; values AFTER B's real collections, proving the mutations survived GC.\n   114\t  (vector-set! w2-witness-obj 0 i)\n   115\t  (vector-set! w2-witness-obj 1 (+ (vector-ref w2-witness-obj 1) 1)))\n   116\t\n   117\t(define (w2-b-rounds n #!optional (handshake-after-first? #f))\n   118\t  ;; n real GC rounds: allocate, mutate the rooted witness object, (##gc),\n   119\t  ;; then the documented C API; optionally call the C release handshake\n   120\t  ;; FROM SCHEME after the first completed round.\n   121\t  (let loop ((i 1))\n   122\t    (if (<= i n)\n   123\t        (begin\n   124\t          ;; the round's observation: did it START while C was blocked?\n   125\t          (if (= (w2-in-block-p) 1)\n   126\t              (set! w2-rounds-during-block (+ w2-rounds-during-block 1))\n   127\t              (set! w2-rounds-after (+ w2-rounds-after 1)))\n   128\t          (if (< w2-a-calls-done 3)\n   129\t              (set! w2-rounds-overlapping (+ w2-rounds-overlapping 1)))\n   130\t          (w2-log \"W2-B: round \" i \" t=\" (w2-now)\n   131\t                  \" start (c-in-block=\" (w2-in-block-p)\n   132\t                  \" a-calls-done=\" w2-a-calls-done \")\")\n   133\t          (w2-mutate-witness! i)\n   134\t          (let ((v (make-vector 200000 0)))\n   135\t            (vector-set! v 0 i))\n   136\t          (##gc)\n   137\t          (let ((r (w2-real-gc)))\n   138\t            (w2-log \"W2-B: round \" i \" t=\" (w2-now)\n   139\t                    \" done (capi-gc-return=\" r \")\"))\n   140\t          (if (and handshake-after-first? (= i 1))\n   141\t              (begin\n   142\t                (w2-log \"W2-B: calling the C release handshake FROM SCHEME after round \" i\n   143\t                        \" (real collection completed) t=\" (w2-now))\n   144\t                (w2-release-handshake)\n   145\t                (set! w2-handshake-called #t)))\n   146\t          (loop (+ i 1))))))\n   147\t\n   148\t(define (w2-witness-intact? n)\n   149\t  (and (= (vector-ref w2-witness-obj 0) n)\n   150\t       (= (vector-ref w2-witness-obj 1) n)))\n   151\t\n   152\t;; ---- control -------------------------------------------------------------\n   153\t\n   154\t(define (w2-control)\n   155\t  ;; A: non-blocking foreign calls; B: real GC rounds must overlap them.\n   156\t  (define (a-work)\n   157\t    (let loop ((i 1))\n   158\t      (if (<= i 3)\n   159\t          (begin\n   160\t            (w2-log \"W2-A: non-blocking foreign call \" i \" t=\" (w2-now))\n   161\t            (w2-noblock)\n   162\t            (set! w2-a-calls-done (+ w2-a-calls-done 1))\n   163\t            (thread-sleep! 0.3)\n   164\t            (loop (+ i 1)))\n   165\t          (w2-log \"W2-A: all non-blocking calls returned\"))))\n   166\t  (w2-reset-state!)\n   167\t  (let* ((t-b (make-thread (lambda ()\n   168\t                             (set! w2-b-executing #t)\n   169\t                             (w2-log \"W2-B: executing t=\" (w2-now))\n   170\t                             (w2-b-rounds 3))\n   171\t                           'w2-b))\n   172\t         (t-a (make-thread a-work 'w2-a)))\n   173\t    (thread-start! t-b)\n   174\t    (thread-start! t-a)\n   175\t    (thread-join! t-b)\n   176\t    (thread-join! t-a)\n   177\t    ;; derive the verdict from the observed state\n   178\t    (w2-log \"W2: observed state: b-executed=\" w2-b-executing\n   179\t            \" rounds-overlapping-a-calls=\" w2-rounds-overlapping\n   180\t            \" witness-object=(last-round=\" (vector-ref w2-witness-obj 0)\n   181\t            \" round-count=\" (vector-ref w2-witness-obj 1) \")\")\n   182\t    (if (and w2-b-executing\n   183\t             (> w2-rounds-overlapping 0)\n   184\t             (w2-witness-intact? 3))\n   185\t        (w2-log \"W2-CONTROL-VERDICT: PASS (derived from observed state: B executed, \"\n   186\t                w2-rounds-overlapping \" of 3 real-GC rounds started while A had completed <3 foreign calls, witness-object mutations intact after real collections; the *** GC: report lines above are the runtime's own collection evidence)\")\n   187\t        (w2-log \"W2-CONTROL-VERDICT: FAIL (observed state: b-executed=\" w2-b-executing\n   188\t                \" rounds-overlapping=\" w2-rounds-overlapping\n   189\t                \" witness-slots=(\" (vector-ref w2-witness-obj 0)\n   190\t                \",\" (vector-ref w2-witness-obj 1) \") expected=(3,3)\"))))\n   191\t\n   192\t;; ---- qualify (the qualification witness) ----------------------------------\n   193\t\n   194\t(define (w2-qualify)\n   195\t  ;; Both participants synchronized BEFORE the foreign call blocks:\n   196\t  ;;   A (the primordial thread) waits until B is OBSERVED executing;\n   197\t  ;;   B waits until A signals entry; then A enters C and blocks.\n   198\t  (w2-reset-state!)\n   199\t  (let* ((t-b (make-thread\n   200\t               (lambda ()\n   201\t                 ;; FIRST action: prove B is executing on the runtime\n   202\t                 (set! w2-b-executing #t)\n   203\t                 (w2-log \"W2-B: EXECUTING on the runtime t=\" (w2-now))\n   204\t                 ;; synchronized start: wait for A's entry signal\n   205\t                 (let wait () (if (not w2-a-entering)\n   206\t                                  (begin (thread-sleep! 0.01) (wait))))\n   207\t                 (w2-log \"W2-B: observed A's entry signal; starting real GC rounds t=\" (w2-now))\n   208\t                 (w2-b-rounds 3 #t))\n   209\t               'w2-b)))\n   210\t    (thread-start! t-b)\n   211\t    ;; A: wait until B is provably executing BEFORE entering C\n   212\t    (let wait () (if (not w2-b-executing)\n   213\t                     (begin (thread-sleep! 0.01) (wait))))\n   214\t    (w2-log \"W2-A: OBSERVED B executing on the runtime (synchronized) t=\" (w2-now))\n   215\t    (set! w2-a-entering #t)\n   216\t    (w2-log \"W2-A: entering blocking foreign call (B synchronized and executing) t=\" (w2-now))\n   217\t    (let ((cause (w2-block 6)))\n   218\t      (set! w2-c-returned #t)\n   219\t      (w2-log \"W2-A: foreign call returned t=\" (w2-now)\n   220\t              \" release-cause=\" (if (= cause 0) \"handshake\" \"deadline\"))\n   221\t      (thread-join! t-b)\n   222\t      ;; derive the verdict from the OBSERVED state\n   223\t      (let* ((hc (w2-handshake-calls))\n   224\t           (hd (w2-handshake-during-block))\n   225\t           (bms (w2-blocked-ms))\n   226\t           (rounds-total (+ w2-rounds-during-block w2-rounds-after))\n   227\t           (consistent (and (= rounds-total 3)\n   228\t                            (= (vector-ref w2-witness-obj 0) 3)\n   229\t                            (= (vector-ref w2-witness-obj 1) 3)\n   230\t                            w2-b-executing\n   231\t                            w2-handshake-called\n   232\t                            (= hc 1)\n   233\t                            ;; a handshake release must have arrived during\n   234\t                            ;; the block, and vice versa (one handshake call)\n   235\t                            (eq? (= cause 0) (= hd 1))))\n   236\t           (qualified (and (= cause 0)\n   237\t                           (> w2-rounds-during-block 0)\n   238\t                           (= hd 1)\n   239\t                           (w2-witness-intact? 3))))\n   240\t      (w2-log \"W2: observed state: release-cause=\" (if (= cause 0) \"handshake\" \"deadline\")\n    30\t *   ./w3.exe phase1-nobeat    serialized entry, heartbeat DISABLED during the\n    31\t *                             worker run (undocumented ___set_heartbeat_interval,\n    32\t *                             lib/os_time.c:937 — used ONLY to isolate the\n    33\t *                             cause of the phase1 crash)\n    34\t *   ./w3.exe phase2           concurrent entry: worker pthread calls Scheme\n    35\t *                             WHILE the primordial thread runs Scheme\n    36\t *   ./w3.exe phase3           owner Gambit thread parked inside a cfun call\n    37\t *                             while the worker enters — the shape under\n    38\t *                             which W4-M4's callback survived\n    39\t *\n    40\t * On a ___SINGLE_THREADED_VMS build there is exactly one processor state\n    41\t * (gambit.h:8625-8628: \"Use direct access to the only pstate\";\n    42\t * ___SET_REAL_PSTATE is a no-op there) and no documented protocol for a\n    43\t * foreign pthread to enter.\n    44\t */\n    45\t\n    46\t#include <stdio.h>\n    47\t#include <stdlib.h>\n    48\t#include <string.h>\n    49\t#include <pthread.h>\n    50\t#include <unistd.h>\n    51\t\n    52\t#include <gambit.h>\n    53\t\n    54\t/* c-define'd in w3-server.scm */\n    55\textern int scheme_w3_add (int x, int y);\n    56\textern int scheme_w3_add_alloc (int x, int y);\n    57\textern int scheme_w3_gc_rounds (int n);\n    58\textern int scheme_w3_spin (int ms);\n    59\textern int scheme_w3_phase3 (void);\n    60\t\n    61\t/* Undocumented heartbeat control (lib/os_time.c:932-948). NOT in gambit.h —\n    62\t   used only to isolate the cause of the phase1 crash. */\n    63\textern void ___set_heartbeat_interval (double seconds);\n    64\textern double ___get_heartbeat_interval (void);\n    65\t\n    66\t#define SCHEME_LIBRARY_LINKER ___LNK_w3_2d_server__\n    67\t___BEGIN_C_LINKAGE\n    68\textern ___mod_or_lnk SCHEME_LIBRARY_LINKER (___global_state);\n    69\t___END_C_LINKAGE\n    70\t\n    71\t/* OWNER-THREAD CONTROL: the Gambit thread that ran ___setup drives the SAME\n    72\t   c-define entries the worker will use. This must succeed BEFORE any\n    73\t   foreign-thread phase; a wrong value aborts the run (exit 1). */\n    74\tstatic int w3_control (void)\n    75\t{\n    76\t  int r1, r2, g;\n    77\t  int fail = 0;\n    78\t\n    79\t  printf (\"W3-CONTROL: owner-thread callbacks through the SAME c-define entries the worker will use\\n\");\n    80\t  fflush (stdout);\n    81\t  r1 = scheme_w3_add (20, 22);\n    82\t  printf (\"W3-CONTROL: scheme_w3_add(20,22) = %d (expected 42)\\n\", r1);\n    83\t  fflush (stdout);\n    84\t  if (r1 != 42)\n    85\t    fail = 1;\n    86\t  r2 = scheme_w3_add_alloc (50, 22);\n    87\t  printf (\"W3-CONTROL: scheme_w3_add_alloc(50,22) = %d (expected 1072)\\n\", r2);\n    88\t  fflush (stdout);\n    89\t  if (r2 != 1072)\n    90\t    fail = 1;\n    91\t  g = scheme_w3_gc_rounds (2);\n    92\t  printf (\"W3-CONTROL: scheme_w3_gc_rounds(2) = %d (expected 2; real collections on the owner thread)\\n\", g);\n    93\t  fflush (stdout);\n    94\t  if (g != 2)\n    95\t    fail = 1;\n    96\t  printf (\"W3-CONTROL-VERDICT: %s\\n\",\n    97\t          fail\n    98\t            ? \"FAIL (wrong values on the owner thread — ABORTING before any foreign-thread phase)\"\n    99\t            : \"PASS (owner Gambit thread drives the same c-define entries with correct values before any foreign-thread phase)\");\n   100\t  fflush (stdout);\n   101\t  return fail;\n   102\t}\n   103\t\n   104\tstatic void *w3_worker_serialized (void *arg)\n   105\t{\n   106\t  int i, r, g;\n   107\t  (void) arg;\n   108\t  /* discriminator FIRST: the allocating shape (W4-M4's callback body) entered\n   109\t     exactly like the trivial add. */\n   110\t  r = scheme_w3_add_alloc (50, 22);\n   111\t  printf (\"W3-WORKER: scheme_w3_add_alloc(50,22) = %d (expected 1072)\\n\", r);\n   112\t  fflush (stdout);\n   113\t  for (i = 0; i < 3; i++)\n   114\t    {\n   115\t      r = scheme_w3_add (20 + i, 22);\n   116\t      printf (\"W3-WORKER: scheme_w3_add(%d,22) = %d\\n\", 20 + i, r);\n   117\t      fflush (stdout);\n   118\t      if (r != 42 + i)\n   119\t        {\n   120\t          printf (\"W3-WORKER: WRONG RESULT %d\\n\", r);\n   121\t          fflush (stdout);\n   122\t          return (void *) 1;\n   123\t        }\n   124\t    }\n   125\t  g = scheme_w3_gc_rounds (3);   /* real collections driven from the worker */\n   126\t  printf (\"W3-WORKER: drove %d real gc rounds (runtime *** GC: reports below with -:d5)\\n\", g);\n   127\t  fflush (stdout);\n   128\t  r = scheme_w3_add (1, 1);\n   129\t  printf (\"W3-WORKER: final scheme_w3_add(1,1) = %d\\n\", r);\n   130\t  fflush (stdout);\n   131\t  return (void *) (long) (r == 2 ? 0 : 2);\n   132\t}\n   133\t\n   134\tstatic void *w3_worker_concurrent (void *arg)\n   135\t{\n   136\t  int i, r;\n   137\t  long bad = 0;\n   138\t  (void) arg;\n   139\t  /* wait a moment so the primordial is definitely inside scheme_w3_spin */\n   140\t  usleep (200000);\n   141\t  for (i = 0; i < 10000; i++)\n   142\t    {\n   143\t      r = scheme_w3_add (1, 1);\n   144\t      if (r != 2)\n   145\t        bad++;\n   146\t    }\n   147\t  printf (\"W3-WORKER: completed 10000 concurrent entries, bad=%ld\\n\", bad);\n   148\t  fflush (stdout);\n   149\t  return (void *) (long) (bad > 0 ? 1 : 0);\n   150\t}\n   151\t\n   152\tstatic pthread_t w3_tid;\n   153\t\n   154\tvoid w3_spawn_worker_nojoin (void)\n   155\t{\n   156\t  pthread_create (&w3_tid, NULL, w3_worker_concurrent, NULL);\n   157\t}\n   158\t\n   159\t/* phase3: the OWNER Gambit thread parks inside a cfun (c-lambda) call while\n   160\t   the worker pthread enters Scheme — the same shape as W4-M4 but with the\n   161\t   worker also driving real collections. w3_park_and_join is reached FROM\n   162\t   Scheme (c-lambda), so the owner's Scheme frame is live and parked. */\n   163\tint w3_park_and_join (int unused)\n   164\t{\n   165\t  void *ret = 0;\n   166\t  (void) unused;\n   167\t  pthread_create (&w3_tid, NULL, w3_worker_serialized, NULL);\n   168\t  pthread_join (w3_tid, &ret);\n   169\t  return (int) (long) ret;\n   170\t}\n   171\t\n   172\tstatic void w3_setup_runtime (void)\n   173\t{\n   174\t  ___setup_params_struct setup_params;\n   175\t\n   176\t  ___setup_params_reset (&setup_params);\n   177\t  setup_params.version = ___VERSION;\n   178\t  setup_params.linker  = SCHEME_LIBRARY_LINKER;\n   179\t\n   180\t  printf (\"W3: calling ___setup from the primordial thread\\n\");\n   181\t  fflush (stdout);\n   182\t  ___setup (&setup_params);\n   183\t  printf (\"W3: ___setup returned; runtime live (___VERSION=%ld)\\n\", (long) ___VERSION);\n   184\t  fflush (stdout);\n   185\t}\n   186\t\n   187\tstatic int w3_phase1 (int disable_heartbeat)\n   188\t{\n   189\t  double saved_beat;\n   190\t  void *ret = 0;\n   191\t  int worker_ret;\n   192\t\n   193\t  printf (\"W3-PHASE1: spawning raw pthread (primordial will park in pthread_join)\\n\");\n   194\t  fflush (stdout);\n   195\t\n   196\t  saved_beat = ___get_heartbeat_interval ();\n   197\t  printf (\"W3-PHASE1: heartbeat interval = %f\\n\", saved_beat);\n   198\t  fflush (stdout);\n   199\t  if (disable_heartbeat)\n   200\t    {\n   201\t      ___set_heartbeat_interval (0.0);\n   202\t      printf (\"W3-PHASE1: heartbeat DISABLED for this run\\n\");\n   203\t      fflush (stdout);\n   204\t    }\n   205\t\n   206\t  pthread_create (&w3_tid, NULL, w3_worker_serialized, NULL);\n   207\t  pthread_join (w3_tid, &ret);\n   208\t  worker_ret = (int) (long) ret;\n   209\t\n   210\t  if (disable_heartbeat)\n   211\t    ___set_heartbeat_interval (saved_beat);\n   212\t\n   213\t  printf (\"W3-PHASE1: worker joined, exit=%d\\n\", worker_ret);\n   214\t  fflush (stdout);\n   215\t  /* p1a-r2 verdict semantics: survival is NEVER a pass. */\n   216\t  printf (\"W3-PHASE1-VERDICT: %s\\n\",\n   217\t          worker_ret == 0\n   218\t            ? \"REFUSAL-NOT-REPRODUCED (worker survived with correct values — undocumented serialized reuse of the single pstate; a nondeterminism caveat, NEVER qualification of foreign-thread entry)\"\n   219\t            : \"UNSAFE-ENTRY-OBSERVED (worker entered but produced wrong values — corruption of the shared single pstate)\");\n   220\t  fflush (stdout);\n   221\t  return worker_ret == 0 ? 0 : 2;\n   222\t}\n   223\t\n   224\tstatic int w3_phase2 (void)\n   225\t{\n   226\t  void *ret = 0;\n   227\t  int spin;\n   228\t  int worker_ret;\n   229\t\n   230\t  printf (\"W3-PHASE2: spawning raw pthread WHILE primordial runs scheme_w3_spin\\n\");\n   231\t  fflush (stdout);\n   232\t  spin = scheme_w3_spin (3000);   /* spawns worker, then allocates ~3s */\n   233\t  pthread_join (w3_tid, &ret);\n   234\t  worker_ret = (int) (long) ret;\n   235\t  printf (\"W3-PHASE2: primordial survived scheme_w3_spin (allocs=%d), worker joined exit=%d\\n\",\n   236\t          spin, worker_ret);\n   237\t  fflush (stdout);\n   238\t  printf (\"W3-PHASE2-VERDICT: %s\\n\",\n   239\t          worker_ret == 0\n   240\t            ? \"REFUSAL-NOT-REPRODUCED (concurrent entry survived this run — two threads shared one pstate; nondeterminism caveat, NEVER qualification; exit 70 and 139 are both the documented refusal-failure)\"\n   241\t            : \"UNSAFE-ENTRY-OBSERVED (concurrent entry produced wrong values — corruption of the shared single pstate)\");\n   242\t  fflush (stdout);\n   243\t  return worker_ret == 0 ? 0 : 2;\n   244\t}\n   245\t\n   246\tstatic int w3_phase3 (void)\n   247\t{\n   248\t  int r;\n   249\t  printf (\"W3-PHASE3: owner Gambit thread parks INSIDE a cfun call while the worker pthread enters Scheme\\n\");\n   250\t  fflush (stdout);\n   251\t  r = scheme_w3_phase3 ();   /* c-define'd: Scheme calls w3_park_and_join via c-lambda */\n   252\t  printf (\"W3-PHASE3: worker joined exit=%d\\n\", r);\n   253\t  fflush (stdout);\n   254\t  printf (\"W3-PHASE3-VERDICT: %s\\n\",\n   255\t          r == 0\n   256\t            ? \"REFUSAL-NOT-REPRODUCED (worker entry survived with owner parked in a cfun frame — undocumented serialized reuse; a nondeterminism caveat, NEVER qualification)\"\n   257\t            : \"UNSAFE-ENTRY-OBSERVED (worker entered but produced wrong values — corruption of the shared single pstate)\");\n   258\t  fflush (stdout);\n   259\t  return r == 0 ? 0 : 2;\n   260\t}\n   261\t\n   262\tint main (int argc, char **argv)\n   263\t{\n   264\t  const char *phase = (argc > 1) ? argv[1] : \"all\";\n   265\t  int phase_exit = 0;\n   266\t\n   267\t  w3_setup_runtime ();\n   268\t\n   269\t  /* the owner-thread control MUST succeed before ANY foreign-thread phase */\n   270\t  if (w3_control () != 0)\n   271\t    {\n   272\t      printf (\"W3: control failed — no foreign-thread phase run\\n\");\n   273\t      fflush (stdout);\n   274\t      ___cleanup ();\n   275\t      return 1;\n   276\t    }\n   277\t\n   278\t  if (strcmp (phase, \"control\") == 0)\n   279\t    phase_exit = 0;   /* control-only mode: stop here, exit 0 */\n   280\t  else if (strcmp (phase, \"phase1\") == 0)\n   281\t    phase_exit = w3_phase1 (0);\n   282\t  else if (strcmp (phase, \"phase1-nobeat\") == 0)\n   283\t    phase_exit = w3_phase1 (1);\n   284\t  else if (strcmp (phase, \"phase2\") == 0)\n   285\t    phase_exit = w3_phase2 ();\n   286\t  else if (strcmp (phase, \"phase3\") == 0)\n   287\t    phase_exit = w3_phase3 ();\n   288\t  else /* \"all\": manual diagnostic only; the recorded runs use one phase per\n   289\t          process so a crash cannot erase another phase's evidence */\n   290\t    {\n   291\t      phase_exit = w3_phase1 (0);\n   292\t      if (phase_exit == 0)\n   293\t        phase_exit = w3_phase1 (1);\n   294\t      if (phase_exit == 0)\n   295\t        phase_exit = w3_phase2 ();\n   296\t      if (phase_exit == 0)\n   297\t        phase_exit = w3_phase3 ();\n   298\t    }\n   299\t\n   300\t  printf (\"W3: calling ___cleanup\\n\");\n   301\t  fflush (stdout);\n   302\t  ___cleanup ();\n   303\t  printf (\"W3: ___cleanup returned\\n\");\n   304\t  fflush (stdout);\n   305\t  return phase_exit;\n   306\t}\n     1\t;; W3 — foreign-thread entry witness (C-driven \"server\" program, the manual's\n     2\t;; documented pattern: c-define procedures + ___setup from C, cf. manual §\n     3\t;; \"The c-define special form\": \"Before it can be used, the Scheme part must\n     4\t;; be initialized with a call to ___setup\", and tests/server.scm).\n     5\t;;\n     6\t;; p1a-r2 REPAIR of review finding F1: BOTH exported entries now declare\n     7\t;; (int int), matching their two Scheme formals (x y) — the P1a fixtures\n     8\t;; declared (int), so the generated C converted ONE argument for procedures\n     9\t;; requiring TWO and the 3/3 SIGSEGVs reproduced a malformed entry fixture.\n    10\t;; scheme_w3_phase3 is likewise fixed to (), matching the C fixture's\n    11\t;; scheme_w3_phase3(void) call (it was (int) against zero formals).\n    12\t;; The Makefile regenerates with gsc -keep-temp and VERIFIES the generated C\n    13\t;; shows ___NARGS 2 for both add entries BEFORE any run.\n    14\t;;\n    15\t;; An OWNER-THREAD CONTROL runs inside every mode BEFORE any foreign-thread\n    16\t;; phase: the Gambit thread that ran ___setup drives the SAME c-define\n    17\t;; entries (scheme_w3_add, scheme_w3_add_alloc, scheme_w3_gc_rounds) with\n    18\t;; exact expected values; a wrong value aborts the run before any\n    19\t;; foreign-thread phase.\n    20\t;;\n    21\t;; A RAW pthread (not created by Gambit, never registered with the runtime)\n    22\t;; then calls the same c-define'd Scheme procedures. Two foreign-entry\n    23\t;; phases:\n    24\t;;\n    25\t;;   phase 1 (serialized): the primordial thread (which ran ___setup) stays\n    26\t;;     parked inside a C pthread_join while the worker pthread enters Scheme.\n    27\t;;     On a ___SINGLE_THREADED_VMS build there is exactly one processor state\n    28\t;;     (gambit.h ~8625: \"Use direct access to the only pstate\"; ___SET_REAL_PSTATE\n    29\t;;     is a no-op there), so the worker is reusing the primordial's pstate\n    30\t;;     behind its back.\n    31\t;;\n    32\t;;   phase 2 (concurrent): the worker pthread enters Scheme WHILE the\n    33\t;;     primordial thread is running Scheme (scheme_w3_spin allocates in a loop\n    34\t;;     for ~3s after spawning the worker). Two threads, one processor state,\n    35\t;;     one Scheme stack chain, one allocator: undefined behavior.\n    36\t;;\n    37\t;; VERDICT SEMANTICS (nondeterminism caveat, per the review): fatal exits\n    38\t;; (70 = Gambit fatal, 134/138/139 = SIGABRT/SIGBUS/SIGSEGV) ALL mean unsafe\n    39\t;; entry — any of them is the DOCUMENTED REFUSAL-FAILURE of this witness and\n    40\t;; none is ever a success. If a run SURVIVES (the worker completes with\n    41\t;; correct values — observed on the serialized owner-parked shapes with the\n    42\t;; repaired two-arg entries, matching W4-M4), that is recorded as\n    43\t;; REFUSAL-NOT-REPRODUCED — an undocumented serialized-reuse artifact, NEVER\n    44\t;; qualification of foreign-thread entry. This witness does NOT prove\n    45\t;; \"unrelated entry cannot be made safe\" (that claim is withdrawn per the\n    46\t;; review); it documents that concurrent entry while the owner thread runs\n    47\t;; Scheme is unsafe on the provisioned build, that serialized owner-parked\n    48\t;; reuse is an un-protocolized artifact, and that no entry protocol exists\n    49\t;; (Q4 of AUDIT.md).\n    50\t;;\n    51\t;; There is NO documented entry protocol for a foreign pthread in 4.9.8 — the\n    52\t;; C-interface chapter documents none, gambit.h declares none, and\n    53\t;; ___vm_resize_pstate (the only processor-creation path) is compiled out\n    54\t;; under ___SINGLE_THREADED_VMS (setup.c:883).\n    55\t\n    56\t(c-define (scheme-w3-add x y) (int int) int \"scheme_w3_add\" \"extern\"\n    57\t  (+ x y))\n    58\t\n    59\t;; discriminator probe: same (int int) signature as scheme-w3-add but the\n    60\t;; body ALLOCATES (same shape as W4-M4's callback) — isolates whether\n    61\t;; allocation changes the foreign-entry outcome.\n    62\t(c-define (scheme-w3-add-alloc x y) (int int) int \"scheme_w3_add_alloc\" \"extern\"\n    63\t  (+ x y (vector-length (make-vector 1000 x))))\n    64\t\n    65\t(c-declare \"void w3_spawn_worker_nojoin (void); int w3_park_and_join (int unused);\")\n    66\t\n    67\t(c-define (scheme-w3-gc-rounds n) (int) int \"scheme_w3_gc_rounds\" \"extern\"\n    68\t  ;; real collections driven from a foreign pthread: allocate + ##gc, n rounds\n    69\t  (let loop ((i 1) (acc 0))\n    70\t    (if (<= i n)\n    71\t        (begin\n    72\t          (let ((v (make-vector 200000 0)))\n    73\t            (vector-set! v 0 i)\n    74\t            (##gc)\n    75\t            (loop (+ i 1) (+ acc 1))))\n    76\t        acc)))\n    77\t\n    78\t(c-define (scheme-w3-spin ms) (int) int \"scheme_w3_spin\" \"extern\"\n    79\t  ;; spawns the racing worker pthread (from C) then keeps the primordial\n    80\t  ;; thread INSIDE Scheme, allocating, for about ms milliseconds\n    81\t  (begin\n    82\t    (w3-spawn-worker)\n    83\t    (let ((deadline (+ (time->seconds (current-time)) (/ ms 1000.0))))\n    84\t      (let loop ((allocs 0))\n    85\t        (if (< (time->seconds (current-time)) deadline)\n    86\t            (loop (+ allocs 1 (vector-length (make-vector 50000 0))))\n    87\t            allocs)))))\n    88\t\n    89\t(define w3-spawn-worker\n    90\t  (c-lambda () void \"w3_spawn_worker_nojoin (); ___return;\"))\n    91\t\n    92\t;; phase3 driver: the OWNER Gambit thread parks inside this cfun while the\n    93\t;; worker pthread (spawned inside it) enters Scheme.\n    94\t(define w3-park-and-join (c-lambda (int) int \"w3_park_and_join\"))\n    95\t\n    96\t(c-define (scheme-w3-phase3) () int \"scheme_w3_phase3\" \"extern\"\n    97\t  (w3-park-and-join 0))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba p1a-mt/witnesses/w2mt.scm; nl -ba p1a-mt/witnesses/w2mt-fixture.c; nl -ba p1a-mt/witnesses/results/w2mt-blocked.out; nl -ba p1a-mt/witnesses/results/w0mt.out'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba p1a-mt/witnesses/w2mt.scm; nl -ba p1a-mt/witnesses/w2mt-fixture.c; nl -ba p1a-mt/witnesses/results/w2mt-blocked.out; nl -ba p1a-mt/witnesses/results/w0mt.out'","aggregated_output":"     1\t;; W2MT — blocking-GC witness on the MULTITHREADED-VM 4.9.8 build.\n     2\t;;\n     3\t;; This is the codex review's step 2 experiment: W2's synchronization repaired\n     4\t;; for a build configured with --enable-multiple-threaded-vms --enable-smp\n     5\t;; --enable-max-processors=8 and started with EXPLICIT -:p2 parallelism.\n     6\t;;\n     7\t;; Protocol (the review's F3 correction, implemented exactly):\n     8\t;;\n     9\t;;   1. The runtime is started with explicit parallelism -:p2 (main.c:46-49);\n    10\t;;      W0's (##current-vm-resize #f 4) trick is NOT used (new processors\n    11\t;;      execute a supplied thunk — setup.c:810-835,992-994).\n    12\t;;   2. Thread A and thread B are synchronized BEFORE A enters C: A waits for\n    13\t;;      B's ready flag before making its call.\n    14\t;;   3. A enters the blocking foreign call w2mt_block (ordinary c-lambda; the\n    15\t;;      C fixture sets an atomic flag and logs ENTER before blocking).\n    16\t;;   4. B polls the atomic flag via a NON-blocking foreign call, and only\n    17\t;;      starts its real-GC rounds once A is provably inside C. B logs its\n    18\t;;      (##current-processor-id) on every round: with A's processor blocked in\n    19\t;;      C, any B progress must come from a DIFFERENT processor.\n    20\t;;   5. Each B round: updates LIVE ROOTED objects (a global vector whose cells\n    21\t;;      are replaced with fresh populated vectors + a global counter), then\n    22\t;;      performs a REAL collection ((##gc) runtime primitive AND the\n    23\t;;      documented C API ___garbage_collect). The runtime's own \"-:d5\" *** GC:\n    24\t;;      report lines are the verbatim collection evidence.\n    25\t;;   6. Only AFTER all rounds complete does B call w2mt_release_handshake.\n    26\t;;   7. The C fixture returns HOW the block ended (0 = handshake-released,\n    27\t;;      1 = C-side deadline fired) — independent timeout detection. The\n    28\t;;      verdict is computed from this OBSERVED state plus the live-root\n    29\t;;      verification, not printed unconditionally.\n    30\t;;\n    31\t;; PASS requires: collection COMPLETING while C stays blocked (reason=0),\n    32\t;; B's rounds executed on a different processor than A's, and the live rooted\n    33\t;; objects intact after the collections. \"A changed crash signature or extra\n    34\t;; Scheme progress alone is not a pass\" (review's standard of proof).\n    35\t;;\n    36\t;; Release/claim bridge: NONE is implemented here. This witness exercises the\n    37\t;; ORDINARY c-lambda foreign call only. See findings: no release/claim\n    38\t;; mechanism exists in the stock 4.9.8 source or headers (the FFI macros\n    39\t;; neither mark the processor absent from GC participation nor transfer\n    40\t;; execution ownership; OP_GARBAGE_COLLECT requires every processor with\n    41\t;; id < ___vms->processor_count to enter the barrier — setup.c:1132-1149,\n    42\t;; 1182-1196, 500-580). Absence of a mechanism is itself the finding.\n    43\t;;\n    44\t;; A Scheme-internal watchdog cannot fire if the whole VM freezes, so every\n    45\t;; run is additionally under the external watchdog.sh (90s).\n    46\t\n    47\t(c-declare #<<c-declare-end\n    48\t\n    49\tint w2mt_block (int deadline_seconds);\n    50\tvoid w2mt_release_handshake (void);\n    51\tint w2mt_a_inside_p (void);\n    52\tint w2mt_noblock (void);\n    53\t\n    54\t/* probe of THIS build's configured maximum (include/gambit.h, substituted\n    55\t   by configure: ___MAX_PROCESSORS 8 with --enable-multiple-threaded-vms\n    56\t   --enable-max-processors=8, vs 1 in the single-threaded provisioned build) */\n    57\tint w2mt_max_processors (void)\n    58\t{\n    59\t  return ___MAX_PROCESSORS;\n    60\t}\n    61\t\n    62\tc-declare-end\n    63\t)\n    64\t\n    65\t(define w2mt-block    (c-lambda (int) int \"w2mt_block\"))\n    66\t(define w2mt-release  (c-lambda () void \"w2mt_release_handshake (); ___return;\"))\n    67\t(define w2mt-a-inside? (c-lambda () int \"w2mt_a_inside_p\"))\n    68\t(define w2mt-noblock  (c-lambda () int \"w2mt_noblock\"))\n    69\t(define w2mt-max-procs (c-lambda () int \"w2mt_max_processors\"))\n    70\t;; REAL collection through the documented C API (gambit.h):\n    71\t;;   ___IMP_FUNC(___BOOL,___garbage_collect)\n    72\t;;      ___P((___PSD ___SIZE_TS requested_words_still),());\n    73\t(define w2mt-real-gc\n    74\t  (c-lambda () int\n    75\t    \"___return (___EXT(___garbage_collect) (___PSP 0) ? 1 : 0);\"))\n    76\t\n    77\t(define (w2mt-now) (time->seconds (current-time)))\n    78\t(define (w2mt-log . parts)\n    79\t  ;; one forced-flush line, so ordering with the C fixture's flushed prints\n    80\t  ;; is exact in the recorded output.\n    81\t  (for-each display parts)\n    82\t  (newline)\n    83\t  (force-output))\n    84\t\n    85\t;; ---- live rooted objects (mutated by B, verified by the main thread) ----\n    86\t\n    87\t(define w2mt-live-roots (make-vector 8 #f))\n    88\t(define w2mt-live-count 0)\n    89\t(define w2mt-rounds-planned 3)\n    90\t\n    91\t(define (w2mt-update-live-roots! i)\n    92\t  ;; replace cell i with a fresh populated vector and bump the counter:\n    93\t  ;; mutations to LIVE objects that must survive every real collection.\n    94\t  (let ((v (make-vector 1000 i)))\n    95\t    (let loop ((j 0))\n    96\t      (if (< j 1000)\n    97\t          (begin (vector-set! v j (+ i j)) (loop (+ j 1)))))\n    98\t    (vector-set! w2mt-live-roots i v)\n    99\t    (set! w2mt-live-count (+ w2mt-live-count 1))))\n   100\t\n   101\t(define (w2mt-verify-live-roots!)\n   102\t  ;; returns #f (ok) or a failure description; checks every mutated live\n   103\t  ;; object survived the collections intact.\n   104\t  (if (not (= w2mt-live-count w2mt-rounds-planned))\n   105\t      (list \"live-count\" w2mt-live-count \"expected\" w2mt-rounds-planned)\n   106\t      (let loop ((i 0))\n   107\t        (if (>= i w2mt-rounds-planned)\n   108\t            #f\n   109\t            (let ((v (vector-ref w2mt-live-roots i)))\n   110\t              (if (or (not (vector? v))\n   111\t                      (not (= (vector-length v) 1000))\n   112\t                      (not (= (vector-ref v 999) (+ i 999))))\n   113\t                  (list \"corrupt-root\" i)\n   114\t                  (loop (+ i 1))))))))\n   115\t\n   116\t(define (w2mt-gc-rounds who n)\n   117\t  ;; per round: update live rooted objects, allocate garbage, then force a\n   118\t  ;; REAL collection via the runtime primitive AND the documented C API.\n   119\t  (let loop ((i 1))\n   120\t    (if (<= i n)\n   121\t        (begin\n   122\t          (w2mt-log who \": round \" i \" t=\" (w2mt-now)\n   123\t                    \" pid=\" (##current-processor-id)\n   124\t                    \" updating live roots + allocating\")\n   125\t          (w2mt-update-live-roots! (- i 1))\n   126\t          (let ((v (make-vector 200000 0)))   ;; fresh garbage for the collector\n   127\t            (vector-set! v 0 i))\n   128\t          (w2mt-log who \": round \" i \" t=\" (w2mt-now)\n   129\t                    \" calling (##gc) — REAL collection requested\")\n   130\t          (##gc)\n   131\t          (let ((r (w2mt-real-gc)))\n   132\t            (w2mt-log who \": round \" i \" t=\" (w2mt-now)\n   133\t                      \" done (capi-gc-return=\" r \") pid=\"\n   134\t                      (##current-processor-id))\n   135\t            (loop (+ i 1)))))))\n   136\t\n   137\t;; ---- control mode: GC machinery works on this MT build ----\n   138\t\n   139\t(define (w2mt-control)\n   140\t  (define (a-work)\n   141\t    (let loop ((i 1))\n   142\t      (if (<= i 3)\n   143\t          (begin\n   144\t            (w2mt-log \"W2MT-A: non-blocking foreign call \" i\n   145\t                      \" t=\" (w2mt-now) \" pid=\" (##current-processor-id))\n   146\t            (w2mt-noblock)\n   147\t            (thread-sleep! 0.3)\n   148\t            (loop (+ i 1)))\n   149\t          (w2mt-log \"W2MT-A: all non-blocking calls returned\"))))\n   150\t  (let* ((t-b (make-thread (lambda () (w2mt-gc-rounds \"W2MT-B\" w2mt-rounds-planned)) 'w2mt-b))\n   151\t         (t-a (make-thread a-work 'w2mt-a)))\n   152\t    ;; A starts first so its foreign calls overlap B's GC rounds (the p1a W2\n   153\t    ;; control was criticized — review F3 — for never actually overlapping).\n   154\t    (thread-start! t-a)\n   155\t    (thread-start! t-b)\n   156\t    (thread-join! t-b)\n   157\t    (thread-join! t-a)\n   158\t    (let ((bad (w2mt-verify-live-roots!)))\n   159\t      (if bad\n   160\t          (w2mt-log \"W2MT-VERDICT: FAIL (control: live roots corrupt after collections: \" bad \")\")\n   161\t          (w2mt-log \"W2MT-VERDICT: PASS (control: \" w2mt-live-count\n   162\t                    \" real collections completed with another thread making foreign calls; live rooted objects intact; the *** GC: report lines above are the runtime's own collection evidence)\")))))\n   163\t\n   164\t;; ---- blocked mode: the actual qualification run ----\n   165\t\n   166\t(define w2mt-a-reason #f)      ;; observed end-of-block state (0 handshake / 1 deadline)\n   167\t(define w2mt-b-ready #f)       ;; A waits for this BEFORE entering C\n   168\t(define w2mt-b-finished #f)    ;; set by B after all rounds + release\n   169\t(define w2mt-a-pid #f)         ;; A's processor id at entry (A cannot migrate while in C)\n   170\t(define w2mt-b-pids '())       ;; processor ids of B's post-observation execution\n   171\t\n   172\t(define (w2mt-blocked)\n   173\t  (let ((t-a (make-thread\n   174\t              (lambda ()\n   175\t                ;; synchronized BEFORE entering C: wait until B is running\n   176\t                (let loop ()\n   177\t                  (if (not w2mt-b-ready)\n   178\t                      (begin (thread-sleep! 0.001) (loop))))\n   179\t                (set! w2mt-a-pid (##current-processor-id))\n   180\t                (w2mt-log \"W2MT-A: synchronized with B, entering blocking foreign call t=\"\n   181\t                          (w2mt-now) \" pid=\" w2mt-a-pid)\n   182\t                (set! w2mt-a-reason (w2mt-block 6))\n   183\t                (w2mt-log \"W2MT-A: blocking call returned reason=\" w2mt-a-reason\n   184\t                          \" t=\" (w2mt-now))\n   185\t                (w2mt-log \"W2MT-A: pid after return=\" (##current-processor-id))\n   186\t                )\n   187\t              'w2mt-a))\n   188\t         (t-b (make-thread\n   189\t               (lambda ()\n   190\t                 (w2mt-log \"W2MT-B: running t=\" (w2mt-now)\n   191\t                           \" pid=\" (##current-processor-id))\n   192\t                 (set! w2mt-b-ready #t)\n   193\t                 ;; BUSY spin (NO thread-sleep!: a sleeping thread's timeout is\n   194\t                 ;; serviced by the device loop of the processor it slept on —\n   195\t                 ;; if that processor is the one blocked in C, the sleep never\n   196\t                 ;; fires and B never runs — observed in the first blocked run,\n   197\t                 ;; see results-nonsmp/ and the first w2mt-blocked.out). A pure\n   198\t                 ;; spin keeps B RUNNABLE so the scheduler must place it on the\n   199\t                 ;; other processor while A blocks. The review's protocol\n   200\t                 ;; requires B provably EXECUTING during the block.\n   201\t                 (let loop ((i 0))\n   202\t                   (if (not (= 1 (w2mt-a-inside?)))\n   203\t                       (begin\n   204\t                         (if (= 0 (##fxmodulo i 20000))\n   205\t                             (w2mt-log \"W2MT-B: spinning t=\" (w2mt-now)\n   206\t                                       \" pid=\" (##current-processor-id)))\n   207\t                         (loop (+ i 1)))))\n   208\t                 (set! w2mt-b-pids (cons (##current-processor-id) w2mt-b-pids))\n   209\t                 (w2mt-log \"W2MT-B: observed A inside C t=\" (w2mt-now)\n   210\t                           \" pid=\" (##current-processor-id))\n   211\t                 (w2mt-gc-rounds \"W2MT-B\" w2mt-rounds-planned)\n   212\t                 (set! w2mt-b-pids (cons (##current-processor-id) w2mt-b-pids))\n   213\t                 ;; only NOW may C be released\n   214\t                 (w2mt-log \"W2MT-B: all rounds done, releasing C t=\" (w2mt-now))\n   215\t                 (w2mt-release)\n   216\t                 (set! w2mt-b-finished #t)\n   217\t                 (w2mt-log \"W2MT-B: handshake released t=\" (w2mt-now)))\n   218\t               'w2mt-b)))\n   219\t    (let ((t-block-start (w2mt-now)))\n   220\t      (thread-start! t-b)\n   221\t      (thread-start! t-a)\n   222\t      (thread-join! t-a)   ;; bounded by C's 6s deadline\n   223\t      (thread-join! t-b)\n   224\t      (w2mt-log \"W2MT: blocked window from t=\" t-block-start \" to t=\" (w2mt-now))\n   225\t      ;; ---- verdict from OBSERVED state ----\n   226\t      (let ((bad (w2mt-verify-live-roots!))\n   227\t            (b-on-other-processor?\n   228\t             (not (memq w2mt-a-pid w2mt-b-pids))))\n   229\t        (cond\n   230\t         ((and (= w2mt-a-reason 0)\n   231\t               w2mt-b-finished\n   232\t               b-on-other-processor?\n   233\t               (not bad))\n   234\t          (w2mt-log \"W2MT-VERDICT: PASS (B completed \" w2mt-rounds-planned\n   235\t                    \" real GC rounds and updated live rooted objects WHILE C was blocked — C returned via B's handshake, not its deadline; B executed on processor(s) \" w2mt-b-pids\n   236\t                    \" != A's \" w2mt-a-pid \"; live roots intact; B's round lines above are timestamped before 'W2MTC: ... RETURNING')\"))\n   237\t         ((= w2mt-a-reason 1)\n   238\t          (w2mt-log \"W2MT-VERDICT: FAIL (collection did NOT complete while C was blocked: the C-side deadline fired after 6s and the RETURNING line precedes B's round-done lines — the GC barrier (setup.c:1132-1196) waits for EVERY processor of the VM, including the one parked inside the foreign call; B's allocation progress alone is not a pass; B's pids=\" w2mt-b-pids \" A's pid=\" w2mt-a-pid \")\"))\n   239\t         (else\n   240\t          (w2mt-log \"W2MT-VERDICT: FAIL (incomplete qualification: reason=\" w2mt-a-reason\n   241\t                    \" b-finished=\" w2mt-b-finished\n   242\t                    \" b-on-other-processor=\" b-on-other-processor?\n   243\t                    \" b-pids=\" w2mt-b-pids\n   244\t                    \" a-pid=\" w2mt-a-pid\n   245\t                    \" live-roots=\" bad \")\")))))))\n   246\t\n   247\t(define (w2mt-run mode)\n   248\t  (w2mt-log \"=== W2MT blocking-GC witness (MT build): mode=\" mode \" ===\")\n   249\t  (w2mt-log \"W2MT: t=\" (w2mt-now) \" start\")\n   250\t  (w2mt-log \"W2MT: vm-processor-count=\" (##current-vm-processor-count)\n   251\t            \" max-processors=\" (w2mt-max-procs)\n   252\t            \" cpu-count=\" (##cpu-count)\n   253\t            \" (scheduler behavior is evidenced by the per-line pid= logs below)\")\n   254\t  (if (< (##current-vm-processor-count) 2)\n   255\t      (w2mt-log \"W2MT-VERDICT: FAIL (runtime has <2 processors — must be started with -:p2)\")\n   256\t      (case mode\n   257\t        ((control) (w2mt-control))\n   258\t        ((blocked) (w2mt-blocked))\n   259\t        (else\n   260\t         (w2mt-log \"W2MT-usage: ./w2mt.exe -:p2,d5 control|blocked\")))))\n   261\t\n   262\t;; compiled exe: the mode is the first non-(-:) command-line argument\n   263\t(let ((args (command-line)))\n   264\t  (w2mt-run (cond\n   265\t             ((and (pair? args)\n   266\t                   (member (car args) '(\"control\" \"blocked\")))\n   267\t              (string->symbol (car args)))\n   268\t             ((and (pair? args) (pair? (cdr args))\n   269\t                   (member (cadr args) '(\"control\" \"blocked\")))\n   270\t              (string->symbol (cadr args)))\n   271\t             (else 'usage))))\n     1\t/* W2MT fixture — blocking-call shape with a C-side completion handshake.\n     2\t *\n     3\t * Differences from the P1a W2 fixture (all required by the codex review, F3):\n     4\t *\n     5\t *   - w2mt_block returns HOW the blocked interval ended:\n     6\t *       0 = released by the handshake (w2mt_release_handshake), meaning all\n     7\t *           of B's GC rounds completed WHILE C was blocked;\n     8\t *       1 = the C-side deadline fired (independent timeout detection);\n     9\t *       2 = unexpected.\n    10\t *     This makes the verdict derivable from observed state, not printed\n    11\t *     unconditionally.\n    12\t *\n    13\t *   - w2mt_block sets w2mt_a_inside_c (atomic) BEFORE blocking, so thread B\n    14\t *     can poll (via w2mt_a_inside_p, a NON-blocking foreign call) and only\n    15\t *     start its real-GC rounds once A is provably inside C.\n    16\t *\n    17\t *   - w2mt_release_handshake is actually called — by B, and only AFTER B has\n    18\t *     completed every GC round and updated the live rooted objects.\n    19\t *\n    20\t *   - All timestamps are CLOCK_MONOTONIC seconds, printed flushed, so the\n    21\t *     ordering of C-fixture prints and Scheme prints is exact in the record.\n    22\t *\n    23\t * The real collection used by the witness goes through the documented runtime\n    24\t * API (gambit.h):\n    25\t *   ___IMP_FUNC(___BOOL,___garbage_collect)\n    26\t *      ___P((___PSD ___SIZE_TS requested_words_still),());\n    27\t */\n    28\t\n    29\t#include <stdio.h>\n    30\t#include <time.h>\n    31\t#include <errno.h>\n    32\t#include <pthread.h>\n    33\t#include <stdatomic.h>\n    34\t\n    35\tstatic pthread_mutex_t w2mt_mu = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;\n    36\tstatic pthread_cond_t  w2mt_cv = PTHREAD_COND_INITIALIZER;\n    37\tstatic int w2mt_proceed = 0;\n    38\tstatic atomic_int w2mt_a_inside_c = 0;\n    39\t\n    40\tstatic double w2mt_now (void)\n    41\t{\n    42\t  struct timespec ts;\n    43\t  clock_gettime (CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);\n    44\t  return (double) ts.tv_sec + 1e-9 * (double) ts.tv_nsec;\n    45\t}\n    46\t\n    47\tint w2mt_block (int deadline_seconds)\n    48\t{\n    49\t  struct timespec ts;\n    50\t  int result = 2;\n    51\t  double t_enter;\n    52\t\n    53\t  clock_gettime (CLOCK_REALTIME, &ts);   /* pthread_cond_timedwait needs realtime */\n    54\t  ts.tv_sec += deadline_seconds;\n    55\t\n    56\t  t_enter = w2mt_now ();\n    57\t  atomic_store (&w2mt_a_inside_c, 1);\n    58\t\n    59\t  fprintf (stdout, \"W2MTC: t=%.6f foreign call ENTERED, blocking on handshake (deadline %ds)\\n\",\n    60\t           t_enter, deadline_seconds);\n    61\t  fflush (stdout);\n    62\t\n    63\t  pthread_mutex_lock (&w2mt_mu);\n    64\t  while (!w2mt_proceed)\n    65\t    {\n    66\t      int r = pthread_cond_timedwait (&w2mt_cv, &w2mt_mu, &ts);\n    67\t      if (r == ETIMEDOUT)\n    68\t        break;\n    69\t    }\n    70\t  if (w2mt_proceed)\n    71\t    result = 0;\n    72\t  else\n    73\t    result = 1;   /* deadline fired: independent timeout detection */\n    74\t  pthread_mutex_unlock (&w2mt_mu);\n    75\t\n    76\t  fprintf (stdout, \"W2MTC: t=%.6f foreign call RETURNING, reason=%d (%s)\\n\",\n    77\t           w2mt_now (), result,\n    78\t           result == 0 ? \"released-by-handshake\"\n    79\t           : result == 1 ? \"C-side-deadline (B did NOT complete its rounds in time)\"\n    80\t           : \"unexpected\");\n    81\t  fflush (stdout);\n    82\t  return result;\n    83\t}\n    84\t\n    85\tvoid w2mt_release_handshake (void)\n    86\t{\n    87\t  pthread_mutex_lock (&w2mt_mu);\n    88\t  w2mt_proceed = 1;\n    89\t  pthread_cond_broadcast (&w2mt_cv);\n    90\t  pthread_mutex_unlock (&w2mt_mu);\n    91\t  fprintf (stdout, \"W2MTC: t=%.6f handshake released by B\\n\", w2mt_now ());\n    92\t  fflush (stdout);\n    93\t}\n    94\t\n    95\tint w2mt_a_inside_p (void)\n    96\t{\n    97\t  return atomic_load (&w2mt_a_inside_c);\n    98\t}\n    99\t\n   100\tint w2mt_noblock (void)\n   101\t{\n   102\t  return 1;\n   103\t}\n     1\t### cmd: ./watchdog.sh 90 ./w2mt.exe -:p2,d5,min-heap=64M,max-heap=512M blocked\n     2\t=== W2MT blocking-GC witness (MT build): mode=blocked ===\n     3\tW2MT: t=1795027884.483575 start\n     4\tW2MT: vm-processor-count=2 max-processors=8 cpu-count=8 (scheduler behavior is evidenced by the per-line pid= logs below)\n     5\tW2MT-B: running t=1795027884.4838 pid=0\n     6\tW2MT-B: spinning t=1795027884.483857 pid=0\n     7\tW2MT-B: spinning t=1795027884.4933 pid=0\n     8\tW2MT-A: synchronized with B, entering blocking foreign call t=1795027884.495018 pid=1\n     9\tW2MTC: t=5862484.823763 foreign call ENTERED, blocking on handshake (deadline 6s)\n    10\tW2MT-B: observed A inside C t=1795027884.495108 pid=0\n    11\tW2MT-B: round 1 t=1795027884.495159 pid=0 updating live roots + allocating\n    12\tW2MT-B: round 1 t=1795027884.495346 calling (##gc) — REAL collection requested\n    13\tW2MTC: t=5862490.828910 foreign call RETURNING, reason=1 (C-side-deadline (B did NOT complete its rounds in time))\n    14\t*** GC: W2MT-A: blocking call returned reason=183us, 1134K alloc,  t=77M heap, 1795027890.501085\n    15\t85K live (W2MT-A: pid after return=0% 0\n    16\t70784+16128)\n    17\tW2MT-B: round 1 t=1795027890.501379 done (capi-gc-return=0) pid=0\n    18\tW2MT-B: round 2 t=1795027890.50144 pid=0 updating live roots + allocating\n    19\tW2MT-B: round 2 t=1795027890.501697 calling (##gc) — REAL collection requested\n    20\t*** GC: 107us, 196K alloc, 77M heap, 91K live (0% 69248+24176)\n    21\tW2MT-B: round 2 t=1795027890.502183 done (capi-gc-return=0) pid=0\n    22\tW2MT-B: round 3 t=1795027890.502266 pid=0 updating live roots + allocating\n    23\tW2MT-B: round 3 t=1795027890.502472 calling (##gc) — REAL collection requested\n    24\t*** GC: 105us, 225K alloc, 77M heap, 99K live (0% 69248+32224)\n    25\tW2MT-B: round 3 t=1795027890.502812 done (capi-gc-return=0) pid=0\n    26\tW2MT-B: all rounds done, releasing C t=1795027890.502874\n    27\tW2MTC: t=5862490.831555 handshake released by B\n    28\tW2MT-B: handshake released t=1795027890.50291\n    29\tW2MT: blocked window from t=1795027884.483789 to t=1795027890.502935\n    30\tW2MT-VERDICT: FAIL (collection did NOT complete while C was blocked: the C-side deadline fired after 6s and the RETURNING line precedes B's round-done lines — the GC barrier (setup.c:1132-1196) waits for EVERY processor of the VM, including the one parked inside the foreign call; B's allocation progress alone is not a pass; B's pids=(0 0) A's pid=1)\n    31\t### exit=0\n     1\t### cmd: ./watchdog.sh 60 ./w0mt.exe -:p2,d5,min-heap=64M,max-heap=512M\n     2\t=== W0MT build-configuration witness (MT build) ===\n     3\t___VERSION=409008\n     4\t___SINGLE_VM=defined\n     5\t___SINGLE_THREADED_VMS=UNDEFINED\n     6\t___MULTIPLE_THREADED_VMS=defined\n     7\t___MAX_PROCESSORS=8\n     8\t___USE_POSIX_THREAD_SYSTEM=defined\n     9\t___SINGLE_HOST=defined (-D by gambuild-C)\n    10\t___SINGLE_HOST_LIMIT=30000\n    11\tpstate-TLS-mode=direct ___tls_ptr (thread-local storage class)\n    12\tmin-heap-bytes=67108864\n    13\tmax-heap-bytes=536870912\n    14\tlive-percent=50\n    15\tparallelism-level=2\n    16\tsmp-feature=ENABLED\n    17\t##cpu-count=8\n    18\t##core-count=8\n    19\t##current-vm-processor-count=2\n    20\tprimordial ##current-processor-id=0\n    21\tW0MT-VERDICT: PASS (MT configuration recorded; no vm-resize used)\n    22\t### exit=0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
