tree, source tree never modified): `p1a-mt/gambit-builds/mt/`.\n     8\t\n     9\t## 1. Configure invocation (review step 1)\n    10\t\n    11\tRun from `p1a-mt/gambit-builds/mt` (empty dir), configure from the source tree:\n    12\t\n    13\t```\n    14\t/Users/sto/workspace/gambit-v4.9.8-src/configure \\\n    15\t  --enable-single-host \\\n    16\t  --enable-multiple-threaded-vms \\\n    17\t  --enable-smp \\\n    18\t  --enable-max-processors=8\n    19\t```\n    20\t\n    21\t- `--enable-single-host` mirrors the provisioned mise build (the mise plugin\n    22\t  passes exactly `--enable-single-host` and nothing else — review Q3), so the\n    23\t  ONLY intended variables vs the provisioned build are the three threading\n    24\t  options. It is code-generation config only, not the cause of single-threaded\n    25\t  VMs (review Q3).\n    26\t- `--enable-multiple-threaded-vms` → substitutes `___MULTIPLE_THREADED_VMS`\n    27\t  into the generated gambit.h (configure.ac:1267-1283; default NO).\n    28\t- `--enable-smp` → selects the SMP Scheme scheduler (configure.ac:1287-1299;\n    29\t  `cond-expand` feature `enable-smp` in lib/_thread.scm:9).\n    30\t- `--enable-max-processors=8` → `___MAX_PROCESSORS 8` (configure.ac:1303-1316;\n    31\t  the value only takes effect with multiple-threaded-vms; default 64, provisioned\n    32\t  build is clamped to 1).\n    33\t- There is NO `--enable-multiprocessor` option in this source (verified).\n    34\t- Compiler: Apple clang 21.0.0 (clang-2100.4.1.1), target arm64-apple-darwin25.6.0.\n    35\t  Configure warns single-host+clang is slow; accepted for comparability.\n    36\t- Build: `make -j8` under a 3600s external watchdog\n    37\t  (`p1a-mt/gambit-builds/build-watchdog.sh`, log `p1a-mt/gambit-builds/make.log`).\n    38\t- Platform: macOS 26.6.2 (Darwin 25.6.0), arm64, 8 CPUs (6 performance cores).\n    39\t- No `make install`; witnesses use this build's own `bin/gsc`.\n    40\t\n    41\t## 2. Out-of-tree build fixes (applied ONLY inside the build tree)\n    42\t\n    43\tGambit 4.9.8's generated makefiles are broken for VPATH builds in two places;\n    44\tboth fixed by writing into the build tree, never the source tree:\n    45\t\n    46\t1. `dummy-gsc-boot` rule copies `gsc-boot.bat.windows` / `gsc-boot.unix` by\n    47\t   bare relative path, which resolves to the build root where they don't\n    48\t   exist. Fix: copied both files from the source root into\n    49\t   `p1a-mt/gambit-builds/mt/`. (The source is exactly at tag v4.9.8, so the\n    50\t   dummy gsc-boot path is the correct bootstrap: the repo's precompiled .c\n    51\t   files are used, gsc-boot is a no-op script.)\n    52\t2. `GAMBITDIR_INCLUDE = $(srcdirpfx)$(rootfromhere)/include` (and the\n    53\t   `$(srcdirpfx)$(rootfromhere)/include/gambit.h` dependency lines) resolve to\n    54\t   the SOURCE include dir, which holds only `gambit.h.in`; the configure-\n    55\t   generated `gambit.h` lives in the BUILD tree's `include/`. Fix: rewrote\n    56\t   those to the absolute build include path\n    57\t   `/Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-mt/p1a-mt/gambit-builds/mt/include` in\n    58\t   `lib/makefile`, `gsi/makefile`, `gsc/makefile` (+ tests, bench for\n    59\t   GAMBITDIR_INCLUDE).\n    60\t3. `_kernel.c:5876` includes `stamp-release.h`, which is a checked-in source\n    61\t   file in the source `include/` dir that the rewritten `-I` no longer covers.\n    62\t   Fix: copied `stamp-release.h` from the source `include/` into the build\n    63\t   tree's `include/` (checked-in release-stamp file, unmodified).\n    64\t4. The flat runtime link file `_gambit.c` is needed in `~~lib` for `gsc -exe`\n    65\t   linking; the build tree's `lib/` lacks it. Fix: copied `_gambit.c` (+ the\n    66\t   symbol table `_gambit#.scm`) from the source `lib/` into the build tree's\n    67\t   `lib/`.\n    68\t\n    69\t## 2b. CRITICAL: the prebuilt lib .c files carry the NON-SMP scheduler\n    70\t\n    71\tThe Gambit git repo at tag v4.9.8 ships PRE-COMPILED `lib/*.c` files generated\n    72\twith the DEFAULT feature set — `lib/_thread.c` in the repo is the NON-SMP\n    73\tcooperative scheduler (no `##thread-schedule-with-acquired-processor!`).\n    74\t`configure --enable-smp` only injects `(define-cond-expand-feature|enable-smp|)`\n    75\tinto `PRELUDE_OPT` (lib/makefile.in:173), which is consumed when the .scm\n    76\tsources are (RE)GENERATED into .c. The stock build's \"dummy gsc-boot\"\n    77\tdeliberately skips regeneration (gsc-boot.unix), so the resulting runtime has\n    78\t___MULTIPLE_THREADED_VMS but the NON-SMP scheduler. An intermediate run with\n    79\tthis configuration is recorded in `witnesses/results-nonsmp/` (thread B is\n    80\tnever scheduled on the idle second processor while processor 0 is blocked in\n    81\tthe foreign call — \"SMP scheduler\" evidence: both threads' pids = 0).\n    82\t\n    83\tGetting the REAL SMP scheduler required a full bootstrap, all inside the\n    84\tbuild tree:\n    85\t\n    86\t1. A plain bootstrap compiler: `boot/` copy of the pinned source via\n    87\t   `git archive HEAD` (in-tree configure + `make bootstrap` inside `boot/` —\n    88\t   the boot copy has no `.git`, so Gambit's own bootstrap path works there).\n    89\t   NOTE: the top-level `make bootstrap` in the OUT-OF-TREE build cannot be\n    90\t   used: the `gsc-boot` git check and `boot-most-recent-release-gsc-boot`'s\n    91\t   `git archive tags/v4.9.8` run inside the build dir, which sits in the\n    92\t   jolt-ffi-mt worktree, so git resolves the WRONG repository and the chain\n    93\t   falls back to the dummy compiler.\n    94\t2. Regenerate the 10 runtime modules (`_kernel _system _num _std _eval\n    95\t   _module _io _nonstd _thread _repl`) with the boot compiler and the exact\n    96\t   `PRELUDE_OPT` from the generated `lib/makefile` (features incl.\n    97\t   `enable-smp` + `##include header.scm`), writing the .c files into the\n    98\t   BUILD tree with explicit `-o`. NEVER rely on the makefile's .c rules:\n    99\t   `gsc -c` writes the output NEXT TO THE INPUT, and the rules pass\n   100\t   `$(srcdirpfx)$*.scm` — a successful regeneration would OVERWRITE THE\n   101\t   SOURCE TREE's checked-in .c files. (An earlier failed regeneration\n   102\t   attempt did truncate 6 source .c files before the process died; they\n   103\t   were restored immediately with `git checkout --` and `git status` was\n   104\t   re-verified clean at the pin before anything else was run.)\n   105\t3. Compile the 10 regenerated .c into .o with the build tree's flags — the\n   106\t   generated `.o` rules hard-code `BUILD_OBJ_INPUT_FILENAMES_PARAM =\n   107\t   $(srcdirpfx)$*.c` (the SOURCE .c), so make cannot pick up the\n   108\t   build-local regenerated .c; the compile is done explicitly, then\n   109\t   `make libgambit.a` re-archives, and gsi/gsc are relinked.\n   110\t\n   111\tVerification: the regenerated `lib/_thread.c` contains the SMP scheduler\n   112\t(91 occurrences of `schedule_2d_with_2d_acquired`); the archived\n   113\t`_thread.o` member matches. The boot compiler itself (`boot/gsc/gsc`) is a\n   114\tplain default-features build and is used ONLY as the bootstrap/regeneration\n   115\tcompiler (`mt/gsc-boot`).\n   116\t\n   117\t## 2c. MT runtime startup/heap fragility (side findings recorded verbatim)\n   118\t\n   119\t- Stock DEFAULT parallelism (0 → 50% of CPUs = 4 here) fails to boot:\n   120\t  `*** FATAL ERROR -- Heap overflow` (gsi and compiled programs alike).\n   121\t  Recorded: `witnesses/results/mt-default-parallelism.out`.\n   122\t- With `-:p2` the default heap boots for small programs; the gsc COMPILER\n   123\t  needs an explicit min-heap (`min-heap=256M,max-heap=1G` in GSCOPTS).\n   124\t- Heap GROWTH under -:p2 crashed the compiler deterministically during\n   125\t  `gsc -exe` of a multi-module program (SIGSEGV in `___H___gvm` on the\n   126\t  primordial thread, data-abort writing near-NULL while processor 1 idles\n   127\t  in the scheduler — macOS crash report `gsc-2026-11-19-003559.ips`);\n   128\t  a large initial min-heap avoids growth and the crash disappears.\n   129\t  Witnesses therefore run with explicit `min-heap=64M,max-heap=512M`.\n   130\t\n   131\t## 3. Generated gambit.h threading macros (review step 1 record)\n   132\t\n   133\tBuild tree `p1a-mt/gambit-builds/mt/include/gambit.h`:\n   134\t\n   135\t- line 1471: `#define ___MULTIPLE_THREADED_VMS` (inside the\n   136\t  `#ifndef ___SINGLE_THREADED_VMS` / `#ifndef ___MULTIPLE_THREADED_VMS`\n   137\t  substitution block)\n   138\t- line 1490: `#define ___MAX_PROCESSORS 8`\n   139\t- line 1527: `#define ___THREAD_LOCAL_STORAGE_CLASS __thread` — and because a\n   140\t  static (non-shared) build does not define `___USE_THREAD_LOCAL_STORAGE_GETTER_SETTER`,\n   141\t  the pstate TLS mechanism is the DIRECT thread-local storage class:\n   142\t  `___GET_REAL_PSTATE()` reads `___tls_ptr` (gambit.h.in:8689-8692), defined in\n   143\t  `lib/os_thread.c:802` (`__thread void *___tls_ptr`), bound only by\n   144\t  `___thread_set_pstate` (os_thread.c:697-708).\n   145\t\n   146\tInstalled provisioned single-threaded build\n   147\t`~/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8/include/gambit.h` (comparison,\n   148\treview step 1 requirement — the macros DIFFER as expected):\n   149\t\n   150\t- `___SINGLE_THREADED_VMS` defined; `___MULTIPLE_THREADED_VMS` not;\n   151\t  `___MAX_PROCESSORS 1` (clamped by configure.ac:1313-1315).\n   152\t- pstate access is the direct static address `&___GSTATE->vmstate0.aligned_pstate[0].pstate`\n   153\t  (gambit.h.in:8607-8612), no TLS at all.\n   154\t\n   155\tThe verbatim header grep for both builds is recorded in\n   156\t`witnesses/results/build-configure.txt` (regenerated by `make record-build-config`),\n   157\tand W0MT reports the macros as seen by a program compiled against the MT\n   158\theaders at runtime (`witnesses/results/w0mt.out`).\n   159\t\n   160\t## 4. Explicit runtime parallelism (review step 2)\n   161\t\n   162\t- W0MT / W2MT (gsc-compiled programs): started with the runtime option\n   163\t  `-:p2` (and `-:p2,d5` when GC reports are wanted) — the gsi/gsc driver\n   164\t  parses `-:p` into `setup_params.parallelism_level` (lib/main.c:46-49,647).\n   165\t- W3MT (C-driven server pattern): `setup_params.parallelism_level = 2` set\n   166\t  explicitly in `w3mt-main.c` before `___setup` — the library-program\n   167\t  equivalent of `-:p2` (same consumed field; `___setup_params_reset` would\n   168\t  otherwise default it to 0, setup.c:4908-4912). GC-report verbosity\n   169\t  (`-:d5` equivalent) via `setup_params.debug_settings = 5 | (1<<4) | (2<<5)`.\n   170\t- The W0 resize trick `(##current-vm-resize #f 4)` is NOT used anywhere\n   171\t  (review warning: new processors execute the supplied thunk,\n   172\t  setup.c:810-835 `start_processor_execution` / setup.c:992-994).\n   173\t\n   174\t## 5. Library/threading-relevant source facts this experiment relies on\n   175\t\n   176\tAll verified by reading `/Users/sto/workspace/gambit-v4.9.8-src` at the pin:\n   177\t\n   178\t- `___garbage_collect` (setup.c:1182-1196) issues `OP_GARBAGE_COLLECT` via\n   179\t  `on_all_processors` (setup.c:1132-1149) which raises `INTR_SYNC_OP` on every\n   180\t  pstate `0..processor_count-1` (setup.c:95-104 `___raise_interrupt_vmstate`)\n   181\t  and enters the tree barrier over `___vms->processor_count` participants\n   182\t  (setup.c:500-580). A processor blocked inside an ordinary synchronous C\n   183\t  call does not execute `service_sync_op` and is not exempt by the FFI macros\n   184\t  (gambit.h:10310-10334 save/restore registers only) — no absence/release\n   185\t  mechanism exists anywhere in the source or headers (grepped: release,\n   186\t  claim, suspend, detach, absent, leave, reclaim).\n   187\t- Runtime-created processors: `___current_vm_resize`/startup creates OS\n   188\t  threads with `start_fn = start_processor_execution` (setup.c:992-996),\n   189\t  which bind TLS via `___thread_set_pstate` (setup.c:819) and then RUN THE\n   190\t  SUPPLIED THUNK (setup.c:810-835).\n   191\t- The primordial processor's OS thread gets its TLS bound inside `___setup`\n   192\t  (setup.c:6383-6406) — so the documented server pattern's owner thread can\n   193\t  call c-define'd functions from C on MT builds.\n   194\t- SMP scheduler: `lib/_thread.scm:9-24` (cond-expand enable-smp branch);\n   195\t  `##startup-processor!` starts thread scheduling on each processor\n   196\t  (_thread.scm:3110-3125); cross-processor C-return guard\n   197\t  `_kernel.c:11743-11755` routes returns via `##c-return-on-other-processor-hook`\n   198\t  → `##thread-migrate-to!` (_thread.scm, SMP branch).\n   199\t- GC scan work distribution and live-word accounting iterate ONLY\n   200\t  `pstates 0..processor_count-1` (mem.c:6269-6280, 6611, 6638, 6678-6702,\n   201\t  6970) — pstates at array slots >= `processor_count` are invisible to\n   202\t  collections run by other processors, and never receive interrupts\n   203\t  (setup.c:95-104).\n   204\t\n   205\t## 6. Deliverable map\n   206\t\n   207\t- `p1a-mt/BUILD-CONFIG.md` — this file.\n   208\t- `p1a-mt/gambit-builds/mt/` — the out-of-tree build tree (NOT committed\n   209\t  except `build-watchdog.sh` + `make.log` excerpt; the tree itself is\n   210\t  machine-local, rebuildable from this record).\n   211\t- `p1a-mt/witnesses/` — witness sources + Makefile + watchdog.sh.\n   212\t- `p1a-mt/witnesses/results/` — verbatim recorded outputs (`*.out`,\n   213\t  `build-configure.txt`, `w3mt-generated-signatures.txt`).\n   214\t- Linux x86_64 leg: PENDING (review step 5 follow-up; not run in this lane).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The r2 suite finishes with `VERIFY: PASS`. I reproduced W1’s 5901 checks with zero failures, W2’s state-derived blocking failure, and W3’s owner control plus surviving serialized entry and crashing concurrent entry. In the MT record, B reaches `(##gc)` on processor 0 while A is blocked on processor 1. I’ll check the attach/teardown claims and timing language next; those need narrower evidence than the overall NO-GO."}}
